The wedge example in the paper.

Inversions are CMP independent 1d inversions at each "trace".
We organise these into separate directories, for simplicity
in running, ability to farm out to a compute-grid, and for some
very simple graphics viewing.

To run, choose the style by editing run_inversions.sh, and
fire off the script:

% run_inversions.sh

Once finished, and you have resp_final and profile_final
files in each CMP directory, a rough view of the whole line
inversion can be obtained with

% csem1DplotSection GeomCMP.txt


Individual fits etc can be seen as, e.g.

% csem1Dplotter CMP3/resp_final

To clean the lot:
% clean.sh
